react
--react is js libary used to build single page applications

react features
1)virtual dom-It is a copy of real dom
             -It will compare and render the changes only using 
             diffing alogorithm and the entire process is called reconcialation
2)components architrecture  -navbar,footer,card,sidebar,jsx
3)single page application-it contains only one index.html

components--It is the piece of code which renders part of ui
1)functional components----Hooks(it is simply like built in functions)

1st component:
function Navbar(){
    return (<h1>navbar</h1)
}
export default Navbar

2nd component:
import Navbar from '/Navbar'

2)class components ---old---life cycle methods

props--properties
-----------------
--It is a object that is used to pass the information from parent to child

--react  will not rerender when the variable changes
--react re renders only when state changes 

State 
====
--It is like a variable it is used to handle the dynamic nature of 
a component or store the data

Hooks
====
--hooks are built in functions that is used to handle react features

1)useState
===========
--It is a hook that is used to manage the state

import{useState} from 'react'

let[state,setSate]=useState(0);

{count}
<button onClick={()=>setCount(count+1)}>inc</button>

Theory
--state--It is like a variable name
--state=1
setSate - it is a function that is used to change the value 
         of a state


htm-routing-anchor tag

single html file- react router dom 
--It is libary in react used  for rounting
-static rounting
-dynamic rounting

steps:
1)npm install react-router-dom
2)configure react router -- main.jsx
import {BrowserRouter} from 'react-router-dom'

<BrowserRouter>
   <app/>  
</BrowserRouter>

3)rules-routes --App.jsx
<Routes>
  <Route path='/' element={</home>}/>
  <Route path='/about' element={</About>}/>
  <Route path='/addnewdoctor' element={</addnewdoctor>}/>
</Routes>

4)Components -navbar
useNavigate()--IT is used for programatical routing

import {useNavigate} from 'react-router-dom'

let navigate=useNavigate()
<button onclick={()=>navigate('/')}>home</button>
<button onclick={()=>navigate('/about')}>About</button>

Dynamic Routing
================
5) <Route path='/doctordetails/:id' element={</doctordetails>}/>  --App.jsx

6)doctor card ---doctor cards
import (useNavigate} from 'react-router-dom
let navigate=useNavigate()

<button onClick={()=>naviagate(`/doctordetails/${id}`)}></button>

7)useParams() -- doctor details
--It is used to get the data from the url

import {useParams} from 'react-router-dom'
let {id}=useParams()


How to call an api
====================
1)using  fetch --- data.json

2)using axios

step1:npm install axios
step2:
import axios from 'axios'
import {useEffect,useSate} from 'react'

step3:
let [doctors,setDoctors]=useState([])

async function getapidata(){
    let response=await axios.get("https://doctorapibackend.onrender.com/doctors")
    console.log(response)
    console.log(response.data)//actual data
    setDoctors(response.data)
}


useEffect(()=>{
    getapidata()
},[])


